            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "[This solution](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/6260c7d3d96efdaaf5dece53457584ece5cf7212/doc/mini-files.txt#L368-L370) works. You can use it to create a mapping like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.files').setup()\r\nlocal minifiles_toggle = function()\r\n  if not MiniFiles.close() then MiniFiles.open() end\r\nend\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>et', minifiles_toggle)\r\n```",
